    "description": "🔍 Grouped search and query operations. Use the "action" field to select the operation.

Common actions: fulltext, semantic, knowledge, check_anchor, query_sql, get_backlinks. Required fields: fulltext: query; semantic: query; knowledge: query; check_anchor: candidates, candidateKind; query_sql: no additional fields; get_backlinks: id.

Additional actions: search_refs, find_replace, search_assets, fulltext_asset_content, list_invalid_refs. Read siyuan://help/action/search/{action} for details, or call action="help" if resources are unavailable.

Parameter contract per action (fields outside the action's optional list should not be sent):
search.fulltext: required [query] | optional [method, methodName, types, typeShortcodes, paths, groupBy, orderBy, sortBy, page, pageSize, parentId, hasTags, stripHtml]
search.semantic: required [query] | optional [paths, types, typeShortcodes, subTypes, page, pageSize]
search.knowledge: required [query] | optional [pageSize, candidateSize, notebooks, paths, types, subTypes, includeRelatedDocuments, activeScopes, namespaceMode]
search.check_anchor: required [candidates, candidateKind] | optional [excludeBlockIds, activeScopes]
search.query_sql: required [] | optional [stmt, sql, maxRows]
search.get_backlinks: required [id] | optional [keyword, refTreeID, scopeRootId, mode]
search.search_refs: required [id] | optional [rootID, k, beforeLen, isSquareBrackets, isDatabase, reqId]
search.find_replace: required [k, r, ids] | optional [paths, types, method, methodName, orderBy, sortBy, groupBy, replaceTypes]
search.search_assets: required [] | optional [k, query, exts]
search.fulltext_asset_content: required [] | optional [query, assetId, queryMethod, types, method, methodName, orderBy, sortBy, page, pageSize]
search.list_invalid_refs: required [] | optional [page, pageSize]

All search actions are read-only except find_replace, which modifies content and requires explicit user confirmation. search(action="query_sql") only accepts SELECT statements; mutation queries are rejected. Because arbitrary SQL can forge result provenance, raw SQL is available only when every configured notebook is readable. When calling query_sql, always add LIMIT yourself. MCP may still truncate large result sets and will tell you when to refine the query. The blocks table columns include: id, parent_id, root_id, box, path, hpath, name, alias, memo, tag, content, fcontent, markdown, length, type, subtype, ial, sort, created, updated. In SQL results, blocks.type uses SiYuan short codes such as d=document, h=heading, p=paragraph, l=list, i=list-item, b=blockquote, c=code, m=math, t=table, html=html, video=video, audio=audio, widget=widget. Requires user confirmation before: find_replace.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "check_anchor": "Use only before writing or changing name/alias, not to locate existing content. Required shape: search(action="check_anchor", candidates=["token"], candidateKind="name"|"alias"). Checks exact normalized tokens before knowledge compilation; name candidates must be globally unique, while alias collisions are reported for semantic or custom-anchor-scope adjudication rather than rejected automatically.",
        "find_replace": "This is the mutating exception inside the search tool. It performs content replacement after write-permission checks and still requires explicit user confirmation.",
        "fulltext": "Pass a query string. Supports keyword, query syntax, SQL, and regex modes via methodName (preferred) or method. fulltext now returns plainContent/excerpt by default. types accepts shortcodes directly: {"h": true, "c": true} auto-expands to {"heading": true, "codeBlock": true}. Use sortBy="relevance" or "date" instead of numeric orderBy. Use parentId to scope within a document, hasTags to filter tagged blocks.",
        "fulltext_asset_content": "Searches indexed asset/OCR text. Prefer methodName and sortBy over numeric method/orderBy. Provide assetId for an exact asset-content lookup.",
        "get_backlinks": "Returns documents/blocks that contain references and/or text mentions for the given block ID. Use mode="links" | "mentions" | "both". Partial permission-filtered results include machine-readable metadata.",
        "knowledge": "Probes the readable controlled namespace before semantic retrieval. One exact name/alias returns locally with trust metadata and no data egress; duplicate exact anchors return an explicit ambiguity unless activeScopes identifies exactly one target; contained unique anchors seed semantic retrieval. Remaining queries use the SiYuan 3.8 embedding provider and may incur cost. namespaceMode="off" is reserved for retrieval evaluation baselines.",
        "list_invalid_refs": "no extra fields",
        "query_sql": "Execute a SELECT statement. Common tables include blocks, spans, assets, attributes, and refs. Prefer sql over stmt when prompting an AI. Always use LIMIT to control kernel work; maxRows controls the returned window (default 200, maximum 1000). Unattributed aggregate rows are returned only when every notebook is readable; otherwise MCP fails closed and reports the omission.",
        "search_assets": "Searches asset filenames. Prefer query over k when prompting an AI. If you need OCR or indexed inner-text matches, use fulltext_asset_content instead.",
        "search_refs": "Returns block-level reference contexts for the target id. Use this when you need the surrounding block content, not just the document-level backlink list. beforeLen controls how much leading context is included in each hit.",
        "semantic": "Low-level semantic candidates from the SiYuan 3.8 embedding index. The query leaves the workspace for the configured provider; verify source attributes before reuse.",
      },
      "actions": {
