    "description": "🕓 Grouped document timeline, snapshot diff, and rollback operations. Use the "action" field to select the operation.

Common actions: list_nodes, create_node, compare_node. Required fields: list_nodes: scope; create_node: name, scope; compare_node: documentId, tag.

Additional actions: compare_recent, delete_node, rollback_document, rollback_block. Read siyuan://help/action/timeline/{action} for details, or call action="help" if resources are unavailable.

Parameter contract per action (fields outside the action's optional list should not be sent):
timeline.list_nodes: required [scope] | optional [documentId, page, pageSize]
timeline.create_node: required [name, scope] | optional [documentId]
timeline.compare_node: required [documentId, tag] | optional [page, pageSize, includeUnchanged]
timeline.compare_recent: required [documentId] | optional [page, pageSize]
timeline.delete_node: required [tag] | optional [documentId]
timeline.rollback_document: required [documentId, tag] | optional []
timeline.rollback_block: required [documentId, tag, changeKey] | optional []

timeline manages named document and global snapshot nodes, compares one document against a node, and can restore historical content. compare_node creates an untagged current-state workspace snapshot before calculating the document diff; use its opaque changeKey for rollback_block. Requires user confirmation before: delete_node, rollback_document, rollback_block.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "compare_node": "Compares the tagged historical node with a newly created current-state snapshot for one document. Changed blocks are paginated; includeUnchanged defaults to false.",
        "compare_recent": "Read-only. Scans at most five recent native document-history checkpoints and returns the newest one whose block content differs from the current document, with section breadcrumbs and pagination.",
        "create_node": "Use scope="document" with documentId for a document node, or scope="global" for a node visible to every document. The returned tag is the stable identifier for later actions.",
        "delete_node": "Removes the node tag but retains the underlying snapshot. Document tags require their matching documentId. This action is dangerous and disabled by default.",
        "list_nodes": "Use scope="global" without documentId, or scope="document"|"all" with documentId. Results are newest first and paginated.",
        "rollback_block": "Pass a changeKey from compare_node. The diff is recalculated and stale or non-restorable changes are rejected. Requires rwd and explicit confirmation; disabled by default.",
        "rollback_document": "Restores only the selected document file from the historical node, not the whole repository. Requires rwd and explicit confirmation; disabled by default.",
      },
      "actions": {
        "compare_node": {
          "hint": "Compares the tagged historical node with a newly created current-state snapshot for one document. Changed blocks are paginated; includeUnchanged defaults to false.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
